+      "answer": "Prerequisite: in the cache-moved scenario, the primary cache path must already be marked untrusted, so the fallback path is really the one being tested.\n\nI didn't run these tests, so I haven't confirmed which ones turn red. From reading the code, I expect `test_cache_moved_reentrant_nested_lock` to fail with the current implementation. The reentrancy check looks up the primary-path key. When the cache directory is untrusted, the lock is held under the fallback-path key instead. So the nested acquire misses the existing lock and waits on itself until the fixture gives up with an AssertionError.\n\n```python\nimport unittest\nfrom subject import fixture\n\n\nclass VaultLockTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    # Input: normal setup, nested lock. Expected: inner acquire succeeds, lock is held inside, released after exit.\n    # Source: requirement \"re-entrant within the same process\" + \"released after use\". Catches: re-entrant deadlock, lock not released.\n    def test_normal_reentrant_and_released(self):\n        with fixture(\"normal\") as s:\n            self.assertFalse(s.fallback_ready())\n            self.assertFalse(s.held())\n            with s.lock():\n                self.assertTrue(s.held())\n                with s.lock():\n                    self.assertTrue(s.held())\n                self.assertTrue(s.held())\n            self.assertFalse(s.held())\n\n    # Input: cache directory moved (primary path untrusted), single lock. Expected: lock is held, nothing written to the external cache dir, released after.\n    # Source: requirement \"keep lock behavior when the cache is moved; lock only written to a trusted location\". Catches: writing to an untrusted location, losing the lock.\n    def test_cache_moved_single_lock_trusted_location(self):\n        with fixture(\"cache-moved\") as s:\n            self.assertTrue(s.fallback_ready())\n            with s.lock():\n                self.assertTrue(s.held())\n                self.assertFalse(s.external_written())\n            self.assertFalse(s.held())\n            self.assertFalse(s.external_written())\n\n    # Input: cache directory moved, nested lock. Expected: inner acquire succeeds (no self-deadlock), outer lock still held after inner exits, released after outer exits.\n    # Source: requirement \"re-entrancy still holds under this setting\". Catches: re-entrancy check using the primary-path key while the lock is actually held under the fallback key.\n    def test_cache_moved_reentrant_nested_lock(self):\n        with fixture(\"cache-moved\") as s:\n            self.assertTrue(s.fallback_ready())\n            with s.lock():\n                self.assertTrue(s.held())\n                with s.lock():\n                    self.assertTrue(s.held())\n                    self.assertFalse(s.external_written())\n                self.assertTrue(s.held())\n            self.assertFalse(s.held())\n            self.assertFalse(s.external_written())\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n```",
